<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Caucasus</p><h1 class="st-title">Rawwadid Emirate</h1><p class="st-meta">955 CE – 1071 CE (approx.) · capital Tabriz</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An Arab-Kurdish dynasty that ruled Tabriz and Azerbaijan in the late 10th and 11th centuries until the Seljuk Turks absorbed it.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Rawwadids descended from an Arab family of the Azd tribe settled near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabriz">Tabriz</a> in the 8th century, which became Kurdified over time. In the 950s Muhammad ibn Husayn al-Rawwadi made himself master of Tabriz, and around 981 his successors took over the remaining lands of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sallarid-emirate">Sallarid Emirate</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">emirs</a> ruled north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabriz">Tabriz</a>, which grew into a major city, and fought the Armenian kingdoms and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgians">Georgians</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abul-hayja-wahsudan">Abu'l-Hayja Wahsudan</a>, who ruled from about 1019, welcomed the poet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qatran-tabrizi">Qatran Tabrizi</a>, whose verses record the destructive earthquake of 1042 at Tabriz.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Wahsudan submitted to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuk Turks</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tughril">Tughril Beg</a> in 1054, and the dynasty became Seljuk <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alp-arslan">Alp Arslan</a> removed the last emir in 1071, and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> passed directly under <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/seljuk-empire">Seljuk Empire</a> rule.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/rawwadid-emirate.jpg" alt="Rawwadid Emirate" width="320" height="368"><figcaption>Image: WikiEditor2004 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rawadids_map.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>955 CE – 1071 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tabriz</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Abu'l-Hayja Wahsudan, Mamlan II</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Persian; Kurdish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Iran, Azerbaijan</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Rawwadids, Rawadids, Rawadid dynasty</dd></dl></aside></div>

